# Slice 282 probe: what the flat two-field receiver holds when its second operand is a named Structure: the place's first value, or nothing.  Entry 7.
Model:
    int: v 4
end: Model
fn: two () int
    return: 2
end: two
fn: run_null () int
    @: x Model
    ---
        return: x\v
        catch: interpreter ()
            return: 55
    ---
end: run_null
fn: run_callable () int
    @: ptr two
    return: ptr()
end: run_callable
int: code 0
int: got run_null()
if: got = 4
    code: 1
---
if: got = 55
    code: 2
---
int: called run_callable()
if: called != 2
    code: code + 10
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code + 100; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
